WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:05.220
Here's a very interesting question.

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:07.120
What is Pi?

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:11.140
Assume we draw a circle of radius three centimeters.

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:13.500
It will look something like this.

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:19.200
As we know this red boundary of the circle will be its perimeter.

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:23.060
We have a special name for the perimeter of a circle.

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:25.900
It's called the circumference of the circle.

00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:29.760
But how do we measure the circumference of the circle?

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:31.720
The circumference is round

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:35.380
and the scale we used to measure any length is straight.

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:36.560
It's simple.

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:38.960
We just place the redline like this.

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:43.580
Like a straight line and measured this length using a scale.

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:46.380
This circumference of this particular circle,

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:50.960
will measure approximately eighteen point eight five centimeters.

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:55.700
It means if we draw a circle of radius three centimeters

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:58.820
and measure its perimeter it will equal

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:01.840
eighteen point eight five centimeters.

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:05.640
Let's also note the diameter of the circle.

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:09.620
The diameter of a circle is two times its radius.

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:12.940
So the diameter will be 2 multiplied by three

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:15.900
which equals six centimeters.

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:17.240
For this circle,

00:01:17.480 --> 00:01:22.300
these are the values we have for circumference and the diameter.

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:26.260
Now, let's draw a circle of radius four centimeters.

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:30.180
This time as well, we measure its circumference.

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:33.940
This red mark will be the circumference and to measure it,

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:36.740
we make the curved line straight.

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:39.700
This will be the length of the boundary.

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:42.920
For this circle we get the circumference

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:47.180
as approximately twenty-five point one centimeters.

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:52.620
The diameter will be twice its radius which equals eight centimeters.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:55.900
So we have the circumference and the diameter values

00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:58.400
for each of the circles.

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:00.620
Now here's the best part.

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:03.260
If we calculate the value of circumference

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:05.360
by the diameter in the first case,

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:09.780
we will come up with approximately 3.14.

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:12.980
What do you think will be the value of circumference

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:15.440
by diameter in the second case?

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:18.100
Guess what! It will be the same.

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:21.480
Approximately 3.14 again,

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:23.920
No matter which circle you look at

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:26.880
this value of the circumference by the diameter

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:31.220
will always be approximately equal to this value.

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:34.280
This value is called Pi.

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:38.680
Remember, both these values are approximations.

00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:42.320
As circumference by diameter equals Pi.

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:45.620
We can say that the circumference of a circle

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:48.840
equals Pi multiplied by the diameter.

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:51.120
If we call the diameter D,

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:55.340
then the formula can be written as, pi multiplied by D.

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:59.060
Which can also be written as pi multiplied by 2R,

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:02.800
because the diameter is twice the radius.

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:07.520
So the circumference of a circle is written as 2 Pi R.

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:09.740
This is a very important formula

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:12.460
as it gives you the value of the circumference

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:16.340
even if you just have the radius of the circle.

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:20.800
There is another important thing about this special constant Pi.

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:25.100
We get the same value if we divide 22 by 7.

00:03:25.460 --> 00:03:28.560
So the value of pi approximately equals

00:03:28.780 --> 00:03:30.120
3.14

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:32.120
or 22 by 7.

